"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nA massive market located in the heart of Melbourne.  \nWith over 140 years of history, it's home to more than 600 small vendors under one roof.\n\nFrom souvenirs to fresh produce to everyday essentials, it felt like you could find just about anything.  \nJust browsing took quite a bit of time.\n\n\n\nI was caught off guard at the vegetable section.  \nEvery single vegetable was enormous.  \nPrice-wise, it was roughly on par with back home.\n\nOne tip: don't buy Australian strawberries.  \nDespite their looks, they just don't taste good.\n\nIt's a fun place with plenty to see and eat, but if you're planning to visit Sydney, there's probably no need to buy things here.  \nOur tour guide mentioned that due to distribution channels, Sydney tends to be cheaper.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"